Fix BD-J JVM search path on aarch64 (Android).

libbluray's meson.build hardcodes java_arch='arm' for the aarch64 cpu family, so
the compiled libjvm.so search paths become lib/arm/server, jre/lib/arm/server, ...
A standard OpenJDK aarch64 JRE image (including the Android j2re-image we bundle)
lays libjvm.so out under lib/aarch64/server, so libbluray never finds the VM and
BD-J titles fail to start. Map aarch64 to the correct 'aarch64' JAVA_ARCH.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -83,7 +83,7 @@
 if host_machine.cpu_family() == 'x86_64'
     java_arch = 'amd64'
 elif host_machine.cpu_family() == 'aarch64'
-    java_arch = 'arm'
+    java_arch = 'aarch64'
 elif host_machine.cpu_family() == 'x86'
     java_arch = 'i386'
 else
